3,Papua New Guinea Traditional Songs (1 Hour Compilation ...Sacred Flute Music from New Guinea - medieval.orgVarious - Sacred Flute Music From New Guinea: Madang / Windim ...Music of Melanesia — GrokipediaWindim Mambu. Sacred Flute Music From New Guinea ... - DiscogsTrans–New Guinea languages - Wikipedia,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z05H4u8ZXNY,"Sep 19, 2025 · Papua New Guinea Traditional Songs (1 Hour Compilation) Tribal Music - Mamuna (Hypnotic) Perfect for: deep focus/work, mindful walking, meditation, breathwork, study, reading, nature... These recordings are of male-only ceremonies, post-initiation music played on two paired flutes, learned during male initiation. Some tracks are accompanied by percussion, whether garamut (slit gongs) or shell rattles. Track titles are generally the place names from which the music was taken. View credits, reviews, tracks and shop for the 2016 CD release of ""Sacred Flute Music From New Guinea: Madang / Windim Mabu"" on Discogs. Traditional Melanesian music is characterized by complex polyrhythmic patterns, often generated through ensemble performances involving stamping tubes and clapping, which create layered ostinatos and interlocking rhythms across regions like Vanuatu, Fiji, and Papua New Guinea. View credits, reviews, tracks and shop for the 1979 Vinyl release of ""Windim Mambu. Sacred Flute Music From New Guinea: Madang Vol. 2"" on Discogs. Trans–New Guinea (TNG) is an extensive family of Papuan languages spoken on the island of New Guinea and neighboring islands, a region corresponding to the country Papua New Guinea as well as parts of Indonesia.",Rumu,Trans-New Guinea
